      "text": "private key\npublic key\n\n\nPublic Key  ---> Encrypt\nPrivate Key ---> Decrypt",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "private key\npublic key\n\n\nPublic Key  ---> Encrypt\nPrivate Key ---> Decrypt",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vn3G7Q4ScdYVk-4m8ck_K",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2172.3006016509134,
      "y": 79586.4932691909,
      "width": 572,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#a5d8ff",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnU",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 926877473,
      "version": 915,
      "versionNonce": 310249514,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1779708211165,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "in our account we will put our\n public key, so that github can\nauthentice us using .\n\nLets say we are pushing code, \nHow it will authenticate, it will generate\na random number and encrypt it using\nour public key and send it to us, we will\ndecrypt that using private key as only private\nkey decrypt that and send to server, server see\nok this is correct message, and now server know\nI am the owner of this account, so now you can push\nthe code this is ssh.\n\n\nHere best part is we are not giving our password\nprivate key to anyone, public key be with anyone.\n\nbut in instagram we have loged in using username and\npassword,we need to remember this password and save\nto database.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "in our account we will put our\n public key, so that github can\nauthentice us using .\n\nLets say we are pushing code, \nHow it will authenticate, it will generate\na random number and encrypt it using\nour public key and send it to us, we will\ndecrypt that using private key as only private\nkey decrypt that and send to server, server see\nok this is correct message, and now server know\nI am the owner of this account, so now you can push\nthe code this is ssh.\n\n\nHere best part is we are not giving our password\nprivate key to anyone, public key be with anyone.\n\nbut in instagram we have loged in using username and\npassword,we need to remember this password and save\nto database.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
