      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bnm",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1963367466,
      "version": 418,
      "versionNonce": 97114742,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1779710169906,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": " Caching is a process of stoting  data in high speed and small sized storage layer.\n    The cached data is stored temporarily in the cache storage for faster access.\n\nCache is small sized memory, keeps recently used and less frequently changin data handy, so that\nwe can fetch it fast next time.\n\nWe cannot make the whole database a cache because cache is optimized for speed, not durability \nor consistency. Cache usually stores temporary data in RAM, which is expensive and volatile. \nDatabases provide persistence, transactions, indexing, joins, and data integrity. Cache is mainly \nused to store frequently accessed data to reduce database load and improve latency, while the \ndatabase remains the source of truth.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": " Caching is a process of stoting  data in high speed and small sized storage layer.\n    The cached data is stored temporarily in the cache storage for faster access.\n\nCache is small sized memory, keeps recently used and less frequently changin data handy, so that\nwe can fetch it fast next time.\n\nWe cannot make the whole database a cache because cache is optimized for speed, not durability \nor consistency. Cache usually stores temporary data in RAM, which is expensive and volatile. \nDatabases provide persistence, transactions, indexing, joins, and data integrity. Cache is mainly \nused to store frequently accessed data to reduce database load and improve latency, while the \ndatabase remains the source of truth.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
